{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/114152-doing-things-with-covers","id":114152,"title":"Doing things with covers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-16T09:54:03-07:00","id":114152,"title":"Doing things with covers?","content":"This was asked before by others, but I wonder if we can give covers or patch covers to humans? I know technically it is made for demons, but I do not see why not. It could be fun and a way to shed low covers that are about to fall apart, get rid of unwanted parts of your cover to replace with something else more desirable, &quot;loan&quot; your cover out to free up for other covers, pass on a found cover to someone else so that person becomes the target.<br /> <br /> Examples. <br /> 1. Your cover has a partner that is an average person. However, you want to &quot;upgrade&quot; your partner to someone who has access to the cities records to look for unusual GM projects, so you want to be close with that person for a while. You convince the persons partner to give up their partner in a patch job. Now, the demon already has a full plate and does not want to add more work with another cover, at the same time, there is already a partner to deal with. So what to do? Buy low and sell high. Find somebody who is tired of being alone, offer them the chance to be married to this lovely person..for a price of course.<br /> <br /> 2, Loan out your cover. So, juggling multiple covers can be a pain. So, maybe you can have someone take over your cover for a while (like a cult member) to free your character up for other things. <br /> <br /> 3, Getting rid of covers that are exposed, this is a quick and dirty trade. You find a sucker, convince them how great your life is and offer to give it to them for a patch job (or something else). Then when an angel comes investigating, the person who took over the cover will act as distraction while the demon sets up an ambush or plans an escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a totally unrelated thought about covers. I was watching the twilight episode &quot;A nice place to visit&quot;.<br /> Wiki: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Nice_Place_to_Visit\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Nice_Place_to_Visit</a><br /> Free on hulu to watch: <a href=\"http://www.hulu.com/watch/440861\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hulu.com/watch/440861</a><br /> <br /> Basically a person dies and meets his afterlife guide. He is sent to a world created from what he thinks heaven would be. Where everything is great, he is rich, women love him, etc. However, it is explained that everything in the world is artificial, even the people, just props created from his imagination. It is a good episode, so I will not spoil the rest for you. I was thinking that, it would be kind of cool to create fake prop people. The GM creates/summons angels/demons, it would make sense that demons (Psychopomps probably) could create artificial people and things. This could be created from patched together soul bits like making a cover, but as an independent entity. Something that is a cross between fetches from changeling and ghouls from VTR. The creation would have a price, they would have to be charged so many (x) time frame to stay functional. What is the purpose? A couple of them.<br /> <br /> 1, sleeper agents, they can infiltrate places and do things while the characters are busy with something else.<br /> 2, backup cover, a demon could absorb them into a full cover, once absorbed they cannot be independent again.<br /> 3, Part of a pact deal, a lot of people do not want real people, they want some idolized version of their fantasy. This would allow demons to create these perfect people.<br /> 4, morale conflict, your basically creating life. In a way this is your child and might create some interesting dilemmas if the character bonds with the creation unintentionally. Also, there is an ironic twist that demons are doing the same thing some of them rebelled against the GM for doing.<br /> 5, loyalty, they are created from the fragments of pacts and &quot;programmed&quot; by the demon (think the tv show dollhouse). Even if the patch person had free will and wanted to rebel, they would still require the demon to survive(charge up), unless it got access to another power supply like an infrastructure, or it hunts demons/angels and collects power from their remains.<br /> <br /> These are just for fun questions and thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T14:34:18-07:00","id":114332,"title":"","content":"I certainly got the impression from descriptions of Tempters that souls/patchworks can be traded, sold, etc easily. Mechanics wise, this is tough to figure out (IE removing the fluff, that lousy partner you mentioned comes down to cover xp you've either spent or not). I like the idea of trading faces, or selling bits of your cover. However, because of the mechanics involved in just literally trading away the contractual papers and giving up covers/xp, I'd try to run it as a Pact. IE the one demon gets cover xp like a pact with a human (he gets the spouse), while the other demon gets something else useful (cover xp or cultists, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}